&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Ripple, we’re building a world where value moves like information does today. It’s big, it’s bold, and we’re already doing it. Through our crypto solutions for financial institutions, businesses, governments and developers, we are improving the global financial system and creating greater economic fairness and opportunity for more people, in more places around the world. And we get to do the best work of our career and grow our skills surrounded by colleagues who have our backs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If you’re ready to see your impact and unlock incredible career growth opportunities, join us, and build real world value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE WORK:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Manager, Finance will be involved in all aspects of local and global operations and will support critical initiatives to facilitate the expansion of the company’s financial infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the International Controller, you will be immersed in all aspects of our operations, working closely with internal and external partners at all levels. Problem solvers are welcome, especially those with commercial acumen. You will play a vital role in recommending solutions and driving strategic decision-making processes. Your organizational skills will be key in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With a genuine curiosity about emerging payment technology and the blockchain industry, you will be at the forefront of innovation, fueling the expansion of our financial infrastructure and contribute to the future of our finance team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial controllership&lt;/strong&gt; - Responsible for the delivery of all Brazilian &amp;amp; Bacen GAAP reporting including implementing accounting processes related to month-end, quarter-end, and year-end close including P&amp;amp;L, Balance Sheet, variance analysis, and management reports, including legacy businesses. This will include ensuring data integrity of the ledger, working with operations and other teams to ensure timely receipt of trading and operational data to prepare financial records and other returns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate (and explain)&lt;/strong&gt; local requirements into Group actionable deliverables, being the bridge between finance, and local providers (auditors, banking providers, tax authorities and others).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
